I had this problem in my current Valkyrie game. Lathia arrived at the
Castle and couldn't find any way across the moat, even though she
zapped a wand of striking at the drawbridge. In the meantime, she
developed a wonderful ability to use polearms (there was a barracks on
the level above) and after a few thousand turns, developing "skilled",
moving up from plvl 16 to 17 just from kills, and finding all kinds of
interesting items from the randomly generated monster inventory and
death-drop goods, she got a scroll she recognized as earth (thank you,
Sokoban) and proceeded to make her way to the Castle tower for a wand
of wishing, which she was able to identify because it was the only room
with where the monsters behaved in a certain manner--she used
telepathy. I'm saving this one for a little while while I think about
what she's gonna do. This is the best I've done with a non-spell
caster. And though she's managed to make it pretty well and far, she
was also able to exercise her available spells during her moat wait,
and there's some thinking to do.
Moral of the story is, given enough patience, and either a =oSD or a
lot of dragons and giants, the game will give you what you need.



